/-
etcd's WAL over the per-byte Linux file extension (`wal`, `walpb`, `fileutil` and the `os`,
`syscall`, `ioutil`, `crc`, ... they call; `notes/wal-fsext-plan.md`, section 8, "Links"), every
proof instantiated with its callees' results. The callees are read off each proof's binders
(`etc/link_walfs.py`'s docstring); a result is generic in the proof's model parameters (`P`, `Mr`,
...). Generated by `etc/gen-link.py --walfs` -- do not edit by hand.

240 results, 220 of them with no hypothesis. The others take, as hypotheses `h_<name>`, the specs
with no proof and the premises on the model parameters (the client's protobuf laws, ...) they reach:
`h_U_Ok` (3), `h_U_SnapCoh` (4), `h_WalDecEnvSupply` (8), `h_WalHsOwn` (3), `h_WalPbIn_CloneHsLaw`
(1), `h_WalPbIn_GetIndexLaw` (4), `h_WalPbIn_GetTermLaw` (1), `h_WalPbIn_IsEmptyLaw` (8),
`h_WalPbIn_MarshalEntLaw` (3), `h_WalPbIn_MarshalHsLaw` (8), `h_WalPbIn_MustSyncLaw` (1),
`h_WalPbIn_NilLaw` (2), `h_WalPbIn_SizeLaw` (1), `h_WalPbIn_UnmarshalEntLaw` (1),
`h_WalPbIn_ZeroLaw` (1), `h_proto_UnmarshalWalRecordE` (7).

`#print axioms` on a result is its trust base (`etc/tcb-report.py`).
-/
